---
description: Use typed declarations for recovered singleton globals — not void* + casts
alwaysApply: true
---

# Typed recovered globals

When a Ghidra global is a **known class singleton** (layout recovered, methods owned), declare and define it with the **real pointer type** — not `void*` with `static_cast` at every callsite.

**Wrong (local cast helper or per-use cast):**
```cpp
extern void* g_pActiveMapOrderContext;
static __inline TMapOrderContext* ActiveMapOrderContext(void) {
  return static_cast<TMapOrderContext*>(g_pActiveMapOrderContext);
}
```

**Required:**
```cpp
// include/game/TMapOrderContext.h
extern TMapOrderContext* g_pActiveMapOrderContext;

// src/game/global_data_tables.cpp
TMapOrderContext* g_pActiveMapOrderContext = 0;

// callsite:
g_pActiveMapOrderContext->FindPortZoneBySelectedTile(city);
```

Apply the same pattern to other recovered singletons (`g_pGlobalMapState`, `g_pDiplomacyTurnStateManager`, etc.) once the owning class exists. Keep `void*` only while the target type is genuinely unknown.

**Array globals** use the same rule — declare in the owning class header:

```cpp
// include/game/TTerrainDescriptor.h
extern TTerrainDescriptor* g_apTerrainTypeDescriptorTable[kTerrainTypeDescriptorTableCount];

// src/game/diplomacy_globals.cpp (outside extern "C")
TTerrainDescriptor* g_apTerrainTypeDescriptorTable[kTerrainTypeDescriptorTableCount] = {0};

// terrain virtual / field access:
g_apTerrainTypeDescriptorTable[slot]->SetResetLevelSlot68(nation, 100);

// TMinor-only tail methods — reinterpret_cast at the boundary (parallel vtables, not inheritance):
reinterpret_cast<TMinor*>(g_apTerrainTypeDescriptorTable[slot])->SetDiplomacyStandingSlot48(...);
```

Never place typed C++ singleton definitions inside an `extern "C"` block in
`global_data_tables.cpp` or `diplomacy_globals.cpp` — that emits C linkage and breaks
the link against C++ `extern` declarations in headers.
